# Prove complete single-pen notebook output

## Scope and existing evidence

Write a multi-page English and Spanish fixture with titles, prose, equations,
tables, and line art on calibrated blank sheets with no manual content repair.

## Finite two-page bilingual single-pen fixture

**Inputs:** a single accepted semantic notebook revision, one-pen capability,
English/Spanish text with admitted glyph coverage, page geometry and
profile calibration, source-owned ink strokes and a blank A4 page per side.
**Output:** a deterministic two-page conceptual notebook with explicit
shape provenance and planned page boundaries; not plotted sheets.

**Page 1 — English, "Motion and energy":** A4 portrait with 20 mm margins,
one 14 mm title at `(25,30) mm`, a 3-line prose block beginning `(25,50)`:
"Motion changes when a force acts. Energy is conserved in a closed
system. Record the units next to each measurement." A source-math line
`E = 1/2 mv²` begins at `(25,85)`. A 2-column table at `(25,105)` has
headers `Quantity | Unit` and rows `Mass | kg`, `Speed | m/s`,
`Energy | J`; its grid is composed from admitted single-pen straight
strokes. Under the table, a simple arrow-free line-art slope and a
labeled resting block occupy a bounded `80 x 50 mm` region from `(25,155)`.
Avoid unsupported photographic content, colors and decorative layers.

**Page 2 — Spanish, "Movimiento y energía":** identical A4 page/margins,
a 14 mm title at `(25,30)`, a 3-line paragraph at `(25,50)`:
"Una fuerza cambia el movimiento. La energía se conserva en un
sistema cerrado. Anota siempre las unidades." Place source math
`v = d/t` at `(25,85)` and a two-column grid at `(25,105)` with
`Magnitud | Unidad`, `Distancia | m`, `Tiempo | s`, `Velocidad | m/s`.
At `(25,155)`, one simple line-art distance-over-time graph uses
single-pen axes and two labels. All intended marks remain inside
`x=20..190, y=20..277 mm` in the design; real glyph extents are unknown.

**Conceptual acceptance checklist:** each page preserves its exact title,
prose, math source, rectangular table topology, and line-art geometry;
semantic order matches pen-stroke order; no silently omitted accents,
colors, figures or math; each page has a distinct output/checkpoint ID;
page transitions require human blank-sheet replacement and re-registration
with no live motion commanded by this fixture. A future compiler must
provide actual stroke extents, no-collision proof, complete bilingual glyph
coverage, bounded speed/pressure, measured calibration, and a validated
operator-controlled page-change protocol.

**Failure example:** if the profile has no admitted stroke for `í` in
"energía" or a title extends beyond x=190 mm after real measurement,
return a blocking `MissingGlyph` or `PageBoundsExceeded` diagnostic with
page/element identity. Do not remove an accent, rasterize unsupported text,
clip ink, silently drop a line or claim a successful live notebook.

**Assumptions and risks:** page and text positions here are conceptual
geometry, not rendered pixels or measured motor paths. Stroke coverage,
layout, exact equation shaping and safe hardware control are unavailable.
No PDF, paper sample, plot or actual two-page run was generated here.
The notebook remains a complete *design fixture* only.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** theoretical first-release two-page fixture, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** English and Spanish pages with title, prose, math, table,
  diagram, page-boundary policy, and explicit refusal cases.
- **Unavailable:** physical output, measured fit, stroke synthesis, plotter
  integration, and real two-page evidence.
